      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-320354",
      ":question/problem": "The equation $(x + 1)^{2} + (y - 3)^{2} = 25$ represents circle $C$. Circle $D$ is obtained by shifting circle $C$ right $4$ units in the $xy$-plane. The point $(a, b)$ lies on circle $D$. Which of the following is a possible value of $a$?\n\n1. $5$\n2. $-2$\n3. $10$"
