      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-320362",
      ":question/problem": "The equation $x^{2} + (y + 1)^{2} = 36$ represents circle $A$. Circle $B$ is obtained by shifting circle $A$ up $3$ units in the $xy$-plane. The point $(a, b)$ lies on circle $B$. Which of the following is a possible value of $b$?\n\n1. $7$\n2. $-12$\n3. $9$"
